# WN22-DC-000390: Windows Server 2022 Deny log on as a service user right must be configured to include no accounts or groups (blank) on domain controllers.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-dc-000390-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 Deny log on as a service user right must be configured to include no accounts or groups (blank) on domain controllers.`
    description `Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities. The "Deny log on as a service" user right defines accounts that are denied logon as a service. Incorrect configurations could prevent services from starting and result in a denial of service.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,user-rights,security-policy,ksi-afr-ads,ksi-iam-apm,ksi-iam-elp,ksi-iam-jit`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-AFR-ADS,KSI:KSI-IAM-APM,KSI:KSI-IAM-ELP,KSI:KSI-IAM-JIT,NIST-800-53:AC-3`
    control_objective `KSI-AFR-ADS,KSI-IAM-APM,KSI-IAM-ELP,KSI-IAM-JIT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> User Rights Assignment >> Deny log on as a service to include no entries (blank).`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_KSI_AFR_ADS `Windows Server implements KSI-AFR-ADS by ensuring no accounts are granted the SeDenyServiceLogonRight user right. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_APM `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-APM by ensuring no accounts are granted the SeDenyServiceLogonRight user right. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_ELP `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-ELP by ensuring no accounts are granted the SeDenyServiceLogonRight user right. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_JIT `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-JIT by ensuring no accounts are granted the SeDenyServiceLogonRight user right. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_AC_3 `Windows Server implements AC-3 by ensuring no accounts are granted the SeDenyServiceLogonRight user right. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `SeDenyServiceLogonRight`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE absent
        exists boolean = false
    STATE_END

    STATE empty_list
        exists boolean = true
        member_count int = 0
    STATE_END

    CRI OR
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF absent
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF empty_list
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
